Source: @PACKAGE@
Section: electronics
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake,
               pkg-config,
               libftdi1-dev,
               libusb-1.0-0-dev,
               libhidapi-dev,
               libudev-dev,
               libgpiod-dev,
               librp1jtag-dev,
               zlib1g-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools

Package: @PACKAGE@
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: openfpgaloader
Conflicts: openfpgaloader, openfpgaloader-rp1pio, @CONFLICTS@
Replaces: openfpgaloader, openfpgaloader-rp1pio, @CONFLICTS@
Description: openFPGALoader with the fpgas.online patch series (@TRACK@)
 openFPGALoader is a universal utility for programming FPGAs. This is the
 fpgas.online build of upstream @UPSTREAM_REF@ (commit @UPSTREAM_COMMIT@)
 plus a patch series that is not yet upstream:
  * rp1pio cable: JTAG through the Raspberry Pi 5 RP1 PIO block (the
    shared librp1jtag0) instead of bit-banging PCIe-attached GPIOs;
  * netv2 / netv2_100 boards with an auto-detected GPIO cable;
  * tt_fpga board / tt_micropython cable for the Tiny Tapeout FPGA Demo
    Board (iCE40UP5K behind an RP2040/RP2350 running MicroPython);
  * fomu_evt_header board: an iCE40 SRAM load as an SPI slave over
    Raspberry Pi GPIO lines, for the Fomu EVT on a Pi header: through the
    GPIO registers (/dev/gpiomem) on a Raspberry Pi 1-4, through libgpiod
    elsewhere. libgpiod measured under the iCE40's 1 MHz minimum
    configuration clock on a Pi 3 Model B+, which is why the registers are
    used there; the /dev/gpiomem path is not yet measured on hardware. A
    load whose clock leaves 1 to 25 MHz stops with the measured rate and
    the board boots its flash again;
  * --flash-info / --flash-info-json: SPI flash JEDEC id, SFDP parameters
    and the flash's factory unique id.
 .
 It installs /usr/bin/openFPGALoader in place of Debian's openfpgaloader
 package. The version @VERSION@ names the upstream base first and the
 fpgas.online patch-set revision after "+fpgasonline.".
